<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moro Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moro Rebellion was an armed conflict from 1899 to 1913 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army and the Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moro-people">Moro peoples</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulu-archipelago">Sulu Archipelago</a> and neighbouring islands in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. It went on after the main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a> ended in 1902, and included the massacre at Bud Dajo in 1906 and the battle of Bud Bagsak in 1913, after which American authority over the region was established.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moro-rebellion.jpg" alt="Moro Rebellion" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Library of Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:American_soldiers_during_the_Moro_Campaigns.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
